# ============================================================
# File:        Caddyfile.template
# Path:        deploy/Caddyfile.template
# Project:     RaceArena — VPS-INSTALL-1 (2026-10-07)
# Description: Caddy's configuration for a single-server install. `deploy/install.sh` fills in the
#              three placeholders and writes the result to /etc/racearena/Caddyfile.
#
# It is the tested configuration of docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "Behind a reverse proxy" (PROXY-PROBE-1),
# with one change: Caddy runs in its own container, so it reaches the app as `app:4000` on the
# compose network instead of `127.0.0.1:4000`.
#   {{EMAIL}}     the address Let's Encrypt writes to about the certificate
#   {{DOMAIN}}    the name visitors type, e.g. racearena.example.com
#   {{TLS_LINE}}  empty on a real server, so Caddy obtains and renews a public certificate itself.
#                 A local test sets it to `tls internal`, as PROXY-PROBE-1 did.
# ============================================================
{
	email {{EMAIL}}
}

{{DOMAIN}} {
	{{TLS_LINE}}
	# Baseline headers (AUDIT-1 D1). The app sends its own (helmet: CSP, nosniff, Referrer-Policy,
	# frame-ancestors); these are the ones only the HTTPS edge can state truthfully. HSTS tells a
	# browser to use https for this name for a year; the Server banner is dropped.
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		-Server
	}
	reverse_proxy app:4000
}
